<title>USA: Sparks said to peg U.S. corn 8.793 bln, soy 2.276.</title>
<headline>Sparks said to peg U.S. corn 8.793 bln, soy 2.276.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Memphis-based analytical firm Sparks Companies pegged 1996 U.S. corn production at 8.793 billion bushels and soybeans at 2.276 billion, trade sources said.</p>
<p>The corn estimate was above USDA's August forecast for 8.695 billion and the soybean estimate was below USDA's outlook in August for 2.3 billion.</p>
<p>Sparks Companies officials could not be reached for comment.</p>
<p>Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8720</p>
